  "dom_id": "step-q349375",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Find $F(t)$ given that \n\n$$\n{F}^{\u2032}(t)=\u27e82{e}^{-t}\\,,6{t}^{2}-2\u27e9\n$$\n\n and $F(0)=\u27e81,\\,-4\u27e9.$\n\n$F(t)=\u27e8${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$\u27e9$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{\u2032}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int \u27e82{e}^{-t}\\,,6{t}^{2}-2\u27e9\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \u27e82{e}^{-t}\\,,6{t}^{2}-2\u27e9\\text{d}t & =\u27e8\\int 2{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int 6{t}^{2}-2\\,\\text{d}t\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-2{e}^{-t}+{c}_{1},\\,2{t}^{3}-2t+{c}_{2}\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $F(0)=\u27e81,\\,-4\u27e9$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0)=\u27e8-2{e}^{0}+{c}_{1},\\,2(0)^{3}-2(0)+{c}_{2}\u27e9 & =\u27e81,\\,-4\u27e9 \\\\ \u27e8-2+{c}_{1},\\,0+{c}_{2}\u27e9 & =\u27e81,\\,-4\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=3$ and ${c}_{2}=-4.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=\u27e8-2{e}^{-t}+3,\\,2{t}^{3}-2t-4\u27e9.\n$$",
